usbiotrace 1.3 (20.09.2024) <graff>
- When printing out port path given as argument the port numbers are now
  displayed one-based as they were entered on command line rather than
  zero-based as they are being used internally.
  (derived from bz#7895)

- Now logs the date and time of starting the tracing session
  (derived from bz#7895)

- Now logs system time with each trace entry
 (derived from bz#7895)


usbiotrace 1.2 (30.12.2023) <graff>
- io_SetupData buffer is now traced at the initiation of Control EndPoint IO
  rather than returning after IO finishes. This allows inspection of Setup
  data for Control EndPoint IO which never completes.

- io_Length is now traced along with IO initiation.

- io_SetupLength is now traced along with initiation of IO to a Control
  EndPoint.

- Now defaults to not tracing the Begin and End trace points. Previous
  defaults would trace begin and end of IO both at USB Stack and HCD level
  which would double the amount of trace entries and usually show the same
  information for both sets anyway. Now only the HCD points are traced by
  default.


usbiotrace 1.1 (04.07.2022) <graff>
- Fixed capture of CustomData from HCD tracing. Previously only the first
  CustomData Name/Value pair would be captured, now all are captured.

- Added PORTPATH=PATH argument for subtopology IO tracing. Requires USB
  stack 53.26 or higher for argument to be used.


usbiotrace 1.0 (01.04.2022) <graff>
- Initial release for use with Sirion USB stack 53.25 or later.
